+# The branch store — 8,852 files that exist nowhere on `main`
+
+**2026-11-05.** Twentieth pass. Previous passes counted refs. This one mirrored the repository and
+measured their contents. **Authority: NONE. Credit: 0.**
+
+---
+
+## 1. What a full mirror shows
+
+`git clone --mirror https://github.com/moxnixmdj/brain` → **229 MB**, then:
+
+| | |
+|---|---:|
+| Refs total | **14,081** |
+| Branches | 6,914 |
+| Tags | **0** |
+| Commits, all refs | **50,042** |
+| Commits on `main` | 21,445 |
+| **Commits off `main`** | **28,597 — 57%** |
+
+Top branch namespaces: `successor/` 877, `breakthrough/` 477, `reconcile/` 379, `repair/` 360,
+`research/` 254, `brain/` 180, `capability/` 154, `truth/` 123, `truth-repair/` 120, `obs/` 119.
+
+## 2. What is in them
+
+Objects reachable only off `main`: **108,485**, naming **11,717 distinct paths**.
+
+Of those paths:
+
+| | count |
+|---|---:|
+| also present on `main` (a modified version) | 2,865 |
+| **exist nowhere on `main`** | **8,852** |
+| total bytes of that branch-only work | **75.0 MB** |
+| median file size | 3,376 B |
+
+Composition of the 8,852:
+
+| directory | branch-only files | for comparison, `main` |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| `canonical/governance/` | **1,968** | 3,219 |
+| `canonical/tests/` | **1,793** | 2,460 |
+| `canonical/runtime/` | **1,643** | 2,335 |
+| `canonical/verification/` | **1,310** | 2,723 |
+| `.github/workflows/` | **416** | 334 |
+| `canonical/evidence/` | 125 | 978 |
+| `execution_guard/` | 25 | 43 |
+
+By extension: 4,439 `.json`, **3,612 `.py`**, 416 `.yml`, 110 `.md`.
+
+## 3. What this means for the answer
+
+Unique file paths across the whole project (`main` ∪ branches, `brain` repo):
+
+```
+main only or shared         16,311
+branch-only                  8,852
+--------------------------------------
+project total                25,163
+```
+
+**35% of the project's unique files exist only on a branch. 57% of its commits were never merged.**
+`main` has 2,335 runtime modules; the branches hold **1,643 more that `main` has never seen** — a 70%
+increase. `.github/workflows/` on branches (416) is larger than on `main` (334).
+
+So the accurate closing statement is not "here is everything." It is:
+
+> **`main` is 65% of the project's files and 43% of its commits. The other 35% / 57% is on 6,914
+> branches, measured here for the first time: 8,852 files, 75 MB, including 3,612 Python modules and
+> 416 workflow definitions that nothing on `main` references.**
+
+## 4. Still outside this measurement
+
+| store | size | why unmeasured |
+|---|---|---|
+| runner's **3,719** branches | unknown | mirroring it is the same job, one repo over |
+| 2,865 modified versions on branches | counted, not diffed | would show how far branches diverged |
+| ≥80,000 CI runs, 9,696 artifacts | counted | API-capped at 40,000 per repo |
+| Drive snapshot | 1 zip | needs credentials |
+
+The runner's branch store is the last measurement of unknown size, and by the ratio seen here
+(3,719 branches vs `main`'s 6,605 files) it is likely comparable in magnitude.
+
+## 5. The one-sentence answer
+
+Nineteen passes enumerated `main` completely and correctly: 22,368 present files, 0 unclassified,
+1,756 citations with zero dangling, 141 bound capabilities of which 27 are measured, a substrate that
+rebuilds from a clean clone.
+
+**And `main` turns out to be the smaller part of the project.**
