+# Capability census — what this machine can actually do
+
+**2026-11-05.** Ten passes indexed *files*, *state*, and *history*. This one indexes **abilities**.
+Source: `canonical/runtime/BOUND_CAPABILITY_REGISTRY_V1.json` (141 bound capabilities, 132 distinct
+adapter modules) cross-referenced against the stored end-to-end measurement
+`canonical/capabilities/true/LIVE_SOLVER_END_TO_END_MEASUREMENT_20261017_V1.json`.
+**Authority: NONE. Credit: 0.**
+
+---
+
+## 1. The headline split
+
+| | count |
+|---|---|
+| Capabilities **bound** in the registry | **141** |
+| Supported by ≥1 measured run | **27** |
+| **Bound but never exercised in any measured run** | **118 (84%)** |
+| Adapter modules backing them | 132 |
+| Autogenerated rather than hand-written | 6 |
+
+**Twenty-seven abilities are real in the only sense that matters** — a deterministic run passed an
+oracle on them, at `$0`, with `model_dependency_count: 0`.
+
+## 2. The 27 that are measured real
+
+All at **100% pass** on the 2026-10-17 record (30 families, 50 instances each):
+
+| capability | domain |
+|---|---|
+| `archive.tar_gz.create_from_manifest`, `archive.verify.tar_gz.gnu` | archives |
+| `auto.pypi.bson-modern`, `auto.npm.dfinity-cbor`, `auto.pypi.msgpack`, `auto.npm.msgpack-msgpack` | binary codecs |
+| `decision.synthesis.typed.stdlib` | decision |
+| `docx.document.create.python_docx` | documents |
+| `json.query.jq`, `yaml.to_json.yq` | query/transform |
+| `math.numeric_expression.sympy` | math |
+| `pdf.extract.text.pypdf` | PDF |
+| `python.source.audit.ast`, `python.tests.audit.unittest` | static audit |
+| `python.fault.localize.dynamic.dataflow.v1` | fault localization |
+| `python.software.repair.loop.test_guided.ast.v1`, `…loop.strict_progress.ast.v1` | program repair |
+| `source.objective_relevance.rank.bm25` | retrieval |
+| `sqlite.table.create_from_json_records`, `…verify_against_json_records` | databases |
+| `xlsx.table.create_from_json_records`, `…verify_against_json_records` | spreadsheets |
+| plus the front-end routes `FRONT_COMPOUND_SENTENCES`, `DETERMINISTIC_EXACT_LITERAL_RESPONSE`, `DETERMINISTIC_LITERAL_JSON_RECORDS`, `OUT_OF_SCOPE_MUST_FAIL_CLOSED` | sentence → action |
+
+Note what is **not** in that list: the entire *software-engineering kernel* the repo is named for is
+represented by exactly **three** measured abilities — AST audit, unittest audit, and two repair loops.
+
+## 3. The 118 bound but unmeasured — where the value would be
+
+| domain | unmeasured | what it would do |
+|---|---|---|
+| `python.*` | **52** | refactor (extract/inline/rename), taint flow, dead code, cross-file edit choreography, mutation-kill, pynguin synthesis, PR realize, merge-conflict resolution, issue→PR orchestration |
+| `software.*` | **13** | CEGIS with z3, grid induction, cross-file repair choreography, evidence synthesis, review-gate composition |
+| `chart.*` | **8** | raster chart reading — axis/unit binding, curve value query, legend-style binding, scene graph, binary phase solvus |
+| `code.*` | **5** | tree-sitter polyglot parse/verify/incremental index |
+| `evidence.*`, `knowledge.*` | **8** | concrete-execution oracles, hypothesis-property oracles, claim/consistency assessment |
+| `image.*`, `web.*`, `git.*`, `shell.*`, `terminal.*`, `orchestration.*`, rest | **32** | OCR, QR, chromedriver render capture, git ops, shell, K-star root assessment |
+
+**Every one of the 13 `software.*` capabilities, all 8 `chart.*`, all 5 `code.*`, and all 4
+`evidence.*` oracles is bound and never measured.** That is the gap between the name on the tin
+("software engineering kernel") and the 27 abilities with evidence.
+
+## 4. The measurement layer has the same defect as everything else
+
+The stored record claims **30 of 30 families at 100%**. Re-running the shipped instrument today
+(`live_solver_end_to_end_measurement_v1.py`, seed `435920808002669906`, `run_complete: True`,
+37 families × 5) produces **47.22% new / 36.67% old, 14 of 37 families**.
+
+The two are not directly comparable — different family sets, 50 vs 5 instances per family — but the
+asymmetry is the point: **a stored record in which no family falls below 100% coexists with a
+reproduction in which 23 of 37 fail.** Nobody has reconciled them. This is the tenth appearance of
+the same pattern: a property declared in a file, and a check that would contradict it living
+somewhere else.
+
+## 5. So: what do we really have?
+
+**Twenty-seven deterministic, verified, zero-cost, zero-model abilities** — file/archive/codec
+handling, document and spreadsheet creation *and verification*, query languages, a numeric engine,
+PDF text extraction, AST and unittest auditing, fault localization, two test-guided repair loops,
+BM25 retrieval, and a sentence→action front end that refuses out of scope.
+
+Everything else — 118 bound capabilities, 84% of the registry, including the whole z3/CEGIS and
+chart-reading and polyglot layers — is **declared, wired, and unmeasured**. Not fake: the adapters
+exist, 132 of them, and 27 have been proven end to end. But unproven.
