+# The one asset that is externally checkable — and when it stopped
+
+**2026-11-05.** Eighteenth pass. Previous passes counted the runner's evidence. This one *verifies* it
+against GitHub, and in doing so corrects two of my own figures. **Authority: NONE. Credit: 0.**
+
+---
+
+## 1. Corrections to my own numbers
+
+| claim I made | measured | note |
+|---|---|---|
+| "2,823 committed run records" | **14** `status.json` + **14** `result.json` | 2,823 is the count of *all* JSON files, most of which are governance state and capsule payloads |
+| "6,652 merged PRs" | **4,144 merged** | 6,652 is all PRs (merged + closed + open) |
+
+Both were inflated by counting a directory instead of the object.
+
+## 2. The verification records resolve to real, external CI
+
+Ten `*_PUBLIC_RUNNER_VERIFICATION_*.json` records exist only in capsules (not on `main`). They resolve
+to **18 distinct workflow runs in `moxnixmdj/verification-capsule-runner`**. Each was queried through
+the GitHub API:
+
+```
+run 37028380726  success  2026-10-02  Verify abductive residual theorem v1
+run 37038410569  success  2026-10-02  Verify Brain P1 V4 residual discharge
+run 37006759313  success  2026-10-02  Verify delegation ceiling acceptance v1
+… 15 more …
+run 36966034129  success  2026-10-02  Verify P1 typed trajectory causal route V4
+```
+
+**18 of 18 exist, 18 of 18 concluded `success`, 18 of 18 are dated 2026-10-02.** One example, checked
+end to end: PR #986 merged 2026-10-02T15:39:12Z, run `37028380726` created 2026-10-02T15:38:15Z,
+`head_sha b8204339…`, job `110908709575`, conclusion `success`.
+
+This is the only class of evidence in the entire project that **a stranger can verify without trusting
+anything the project says**. It is not self-attestation; it points at an independently observable CI
+run in a separate repository. And the record carries the right rule:
+
+> `VERIFICATION_APPLIES_ONLY_TO_EXACT_LISTED_BLOBS__ANY_SEMANTIC_BYTE_CHANGE_REQUIRES_REVERIFICATION`
+
+That is precisely the discipline the rest of the project lacks — and here it is written down and
+enforced by blob pins.
+
+The runner executed **40,000 workflow runs** in total. The apparatus is substantial and it works.
+
+## 3. The finding: it stopped 23 days before the last commit
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Runner's last push | **2026-10-12T06:24:31Z** |
+| `brain`'s last push | **2026-11-04T23:08:10Z** |
+| Merged PRs in `brain` since the runner went quiet | **1,782** |
+| Merged PRs total | 4,144 |
+
+**43% of the project's entire merge history happened after the independent verifier last ran.**
+All 18 externally-verified records are from a single day, 2026-10-02. The runner's final runs on
+2026-10-12 include failures (`Verify Unknown-Domain V6 total string route`, `verify-rank26-exact-surface`)
+alongside successes — and then it stops.
+
+So everything merged after 2026-10-12 — the last 1,782 PRs, including every retraction, every new
+capability, the 403rd capsule, the acceptance apparatus described in
+`ACCEPTANCE_DRIFT_20261105_V1.md` — rests on **internal claims only**. The one mechanism that could
+have caught the drift described in the previous reports had already been switched off.
+
+## 4. Why this is the answer to "everything in the whole project"
+
+The project contains a great deal: 22,916 tracked files across two repositories, 403 capsules, 1,089
+workflow definitions, 40,000 CI runs, 141 bound capabilities, 27 measured ones, a hash-pinned
+substrate that rebuilds from a clean clone, and an evidence graph with zero dangling citations.
+
+But there is exactly **one** asset whose value does not depend on believing the project about itself:
+**the public-runner verification protocol**, because its claims resolve to runs anyone can query.
+
+And it is the asset that has been unused for 43% of the project's history.
+
+**The most valuable thing here is not a capability. It is a checking procedure — and the highest-value
+action available is to point it at what has accumulated since it last ran.**
