+# Reference integrity — what the project points at that does not exist
+
+**2026-11-05.** Fifteenth pass. The partition proved every *present* file is classified. This measures
+the opposite relation: every path the project **claims exists**. A citation is a claim about the tree,
+and citations can be checked mechanically. **Authority: NONE. Credit: 0.**
+
+---
+
+## 1. The evidence graph that matters is clean
+
+All 780 action intents, every `progress_evidence_paths` / `evidence_paths` entry:
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Citations | **1,756** |
+| Distinct paths | **526** |
+| **Paths that do not exist** | **0 (0.0%)** |
+
+Every evidence citation in the activity ledger resolves. This is the first property measured in
+fifteen passes that has **no gap at all** — and it is checkable in under a second, which is presumably
+why it holds.
+
+## 2. The governance layer is not clean
+
+Same check over `canonical/governance/*.json` + `canonical/verification/*.json` (5,882 files):
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Path-like references | **42,413** |
+| Distinct references that point at nothing | **878 (2.1%)** |
+
+Some are legitimately external subjects — `data/IFBench_test.json`, `livebench/if_runner/ifbench/
+instructions.py`, `benchmark_releases/osworld-v2.1.json` are downloaded benchmarks, not project files.
+The rest are rot, and a few are load-bearing:
+
+| refs | path | status |
+|---:|---|---|
+| 11 | `execution_guard/CURRENT_TERMINAL_EXECUTION_SURFACE_V1.json` | **never existed** |
+| 9 | `execution_guard/CURRENT_VERIFIED_EXECUTION_INVARIANTS_V1.json` | absent |
+| 8 | `execution_guard/terminal_execution_admission_v2.py` | absent |
+| 21 | `canonical/evidence/FIBO_Q2_2026_FULL_RELEASE_BOUNDED_SOURCE_V1.json` | absent |
+
+`execution_guard/` holds 71 real files — `actions_admission.py`, `live_solver_end_to_end_measurement_v1.py`,
+`enforce_load_bearing_primary_pr.py` and so on. The three cited above are not among them and were
+never renamed into them. **Governance documents cite a guard surface that does not exist.**
+
+## 3. A one-character defect, 87 files wide
+
+The single largest rot class is not a missing file. It is a missing dot:
+
+```
+cited as:  github/workflows/verify-unified-cognitive-fabric-v1.yml
+actual:    .github/workflows/verify-unified-cognitive-fabric-v1.yml
+```
+
+**87 governance JSON files write `github/workflows/` without the leading dot.** None of those
+references can ever resolve, and each one silently fails an existence check that nobody runs. Nine
+references per workflow file in the worst case.
+
+## 4. The tree only grows — which is why none of this is ever cleaned
+
+File counts at four commits (GitHub tree API):
+
+```
+2026-09-20      3 files
+2026-10-05  6,198
+2026-10-20 14,733
+2026-11-05 16,311
+```
+
+**Growth 291 files/day. Removal 11/day** — and 96% of all removals since 10-20 are one vendored
+`real_env/target` copy of `requests`, not project material. Since 2026-10-05 exactly **51 files** have
+been deleted, of which **1** is Python.
+
+So the tree is effectively **monotonic**: at no point has anything been pruned. That is the mechanism
+behind every previous finding — 19 root documents claiming to be THE answer coexist because nothing
+removes the superseded 18; 3,219 governance files accumulate at ~57/day; 85% of disk bytes are
+uncited state because nothing garbage-collects. **"All of them" is now a superset of "all of them" at
+every earlier moment**, and that is a property of the process, not of any one census.
+
+## 5. Where the answer now closes
+
+Four independent axes, each measured rather than asserted:
+
+| axis | result |
+|---|---|
+| Files present | 22,368 → partitioned, **0 unclassified** |
+| Evidence citations | 1,756 → **0 dangling** |
+| Governance references | 42,413 → **878 dangling (2.1%)**, incl. 87 one-character typos |
+| Deletions | 51 since 10-05 — the project does not prune |
+
+Nothing larger is missing. What remains is **rot inside the set**, and it is small, mechanical, and
+fixable: 878 unresolvable references, of which 87 need a single character prepended.
