+# How to run this — verified from a clean clone
+
+**2026-11-05.** Sixteen passes inventoried what exists. This tests the one property that decides
+whether any of it is an asset: **can a stranger reproduce it?** Every command below was executed, in
+order, from a fresh `git clone` and a fresh virtualenv. Results are what actually happened.
+
+This document did not exist. The repository has **136 root Markdown files, 19 of which claim to be the
+answer, and no installation or run instructions anywhere** — `INSTALL`, `QUICKSTART`, `CONTRIBUTING`
+are all absent, and `README.md`'s nine sections are entirely governance (objective, prohibitions, law,
+traps, merge rule). Reproducibility was present but undiscoverable.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Verified recipe
+
+```bash
+git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/moxnixmdj/brain
+cd brain
+git ls-files | wc -l                      # 16311
+python3 -m venv .venv
+.venv/bin/python -m pip install --upgrade pip
+.venv/bin/python -m pip install --require-hashes \
+    -r requirements/software_engineering_kernel_v1.txt
+```
+
+**Verified:** installs clean, exit 0. `requirements/software_engineering_kernel_v1.txt` is 326 lines,
+every wheel pinned by exact version **and** SHA-256 (`attrs`, `cattrs`, `crosshair-tool`, `hypothesis`,
+`tree-sitter`, `z3-solver`, …). This is the strongest reproducibility property in the project and it
+holds: the substrate rebuilds byte-identically on demand.
+
+## 2. Verify the checkout is self-consistent
+
+```bash
+.venv/bin/python execution_guard/repo_integrity_guard_v1.py
+```
+
+**Verified:** `mode=static+diff base=6db8a643bd462cf94bea807c72e7eb5460ad1edd rules=17 violations=0 -> PASS`
+on a pristine clone.
+
+## 3. Run the compression/creature evidence
+
+```bash
+.venv/bin/python -m pytest \
+  canonical/tests/test_r3_real_structural_compounding_cycle_v1.py \
+  canonical/tests/test_r3_second_family_grounding_compounding_cycle_v1.py \
+  canonical/tests/test_r3_third_family_decision_compounding_cycle_v1.py \
+  canonical/tests/test_compounding_and_goal_identity_v1.py \
+  canonical/tests/test_meta_circular_global_sentient_creature_v1.py \
+  -q
+```
+
+**Verified:** `45 passed, 1 warning in 6.47s`.
+
+## 4. What does **not** work, and you should know before you try
+
+| attempt | outcome |
+|---|---|
+| `pytest canonical/tests` as a directory | **never terminates.** Reaches 99% in ~25 min, then hangs; xdist worker restarts duplicate outcomes. ~990 failures ≈ 5.3% among ~15,900 reported. |
+| collection | **42 test files fail to import** (`--continue-on-collection-errors` needed) |
+| running the suite writes litter | ~470 checkpoint/`gz*` files into tracked directories; `.gitignore` documents this, and warns `git add -A` would commit them as evidence |
+| the R4 / root-theorem acceptance path | **7 of 54 tests fail closed** on mission-blob staleness — see `ACCEPTANCE_DRIFT_20261105_V1.md` |
+
+**So: no CI job anywhere runs the test suite.** 334 workflows exist in this repo, 53 invoke `pytest`,
+and all 53 name 1–3 hand-picked files. `pytest canonical/tests` as a directory: **0 invocations.**
+
+## 5. Additions to this recipe that were needed but not documented
+
+- `-p no:cacheprovider` and `--continue-on-collection-errors` are effectively mandatory.
+- `-o addopts=""` was required in this environment; the configured `addopts` otherwise interfere.
+- On a 2-core machine use `-n 2`, not `-n 8` — more workers make it slower, not faster.
+- Nothing documents that a depth-1 clone hides the merge history (`git log` shows one squashed
+  commit); use `gh` for history. 6,652 merged PRs are invisible to `git`.
+
+## 6. Verdict
+
+**The project is reproducible and undocumented.** A stranger with a network connection and the pinned
+requirements can install the substrate, verify the checkout, and reproduce 45 passing tests plus a
+PASSing referee — in about two minutes of wall clock. Nothing tells them so.
+
+That is a different kind of value than everything measured in the previous fifteen passes: not
+"what exists", but **"what survives being handed to someone else."** For the pinned substrate and the
+core evidence, the answer is yes. For the full test suite, the answer is no — it cannot be run to
+completion even here.
