+# State census — what the machine has actually accumulated
+
+**2026-11-05.** Seventh pass. The six earlier reports covered code, evidence, measurement and history.
+**None of them ever opened the persistent state** — the thing that would make every other asset
+compound. This does. **Authority: NONE.** Credit: 0. `truth.achieved` remains `false`.
+
+---
+
+## 1. The complete accumulated learning in a 20,000-file, 6,652-merge system
+
+| Store | Path | Content |
+|---|---|---|
+| Experience cells | `canonical/runtime/state/experience_v1.json` (12.7 KB) | **37 cells**, **0 resolutions** |
+| Associative memory | `canonical/astra_runtime/state/ASSOCIATIVE_MEMORY_V1.json` (7.0 KB) | **12 entries** |
+| Compiled workflow skills | `canonical/astra_runtime/tmp/compiled_workflows_v1.sqlite` | **0 rows** |
+| Routing disqualifications | `canonical/astra_runtime/tmp/upstream_routing_ledger_v1.sqlite` | **0 rows** |
+| Verified route promotions | same | **3 rows** |
+| Verified capabilities (projection) | `canonical/astra_runtime/tmp/VERIFIED_CAPABILITIES.sqlite` | 17 rows — a subset of the 141-entry registry, not new state |
+| Learned rules shipped | instant-learning bundle | 5 rules (python / go / typescript / rust) |
+| Internalized skills | `canonical/capabilities/internalized/` | 18, and **not wired**: `ACTIVE_VERIFIED_LEARNED_SKILL: 0` |
+
+**Total accumulated, persistent, machine-authored learning: roughly 50 records.** Against 151,510
+lines of Python, 3,219 governance JSON, 780 action intents, 1,104 mission receipts and 595
+verification records.
+
+This is the fact that explains the previous six passes. The repository's value is concentrated almost
+entirely in **machinery** — and machinery is unbounded in kind, so every sweep finds more of it. The
+one asset class whose value would *compound* holds ~50 rows. That is also the measured reason
+compounding reads 0/10 and the live solver plateaus at 47.22%.
+
+## 2. The defect this exposes: three quarters of the memory is dead pointers
+
+Of the 12 associative-memory entries, **9 point at `/tmp/brain-cli-reg-*/regme` temp directories that
+no longer exist**:
+
+```
+m10  accesses=12953  blamed=1563  credited=3207  -> /tmp/brain-cli-reg-770jz7z_/regme ...
+m11  accesses=13274  blamed=1453  credited=3313  -> /tmp/brain-cli-reg-pwvlvpyc/regme ...
+m12  accesses=12678  blamed=1354  credited=3025  -> /tmp/brain-cli-reg-9jf32zeb/regme ...
+m4   accesses= 3803  blamed= 225  credited=1322  -> add ten            (resolvable)
+m8   accesses= 1098  blamed=  18  credited= 501  -> rewrite the malformed def  (resolvable)
+```
+
+Nine entries carry roughly **70,000 accesses and 14,000 credits** against paths that cannot resolve.
+The memory keeps scoring them as though they had been used. So the accumulated state is not merely
+small — the small part that exists is **75% unverifiable by construction**, and nothing in the tree
+refuses to credit an entry whose referent is gone.
+
+That is the same defect class the project keeps finding elsewhere — *a check affirming when it should
+have stayed silent* — now in the memory layer, and it is measurable in six lines.
+
+## 2b. The second repository — 403 frozen full-system snapshots (correction to §3)
+
+Earlier reports called `moxnixmdj/verification-capsule-runner` a 30 MB companion and moved on.
+It was never opened. It is the **other half of the system**:
+
+| | count |
+|---|---|
+| Frozen capsules, each a versioned snapshot of the runtime | **403** |
+| GitHub Actions workflows | **1,089** |
+| Python files / lines | 2,599 / **480,325** (vs `brain`'s 151,510) |
+| Committed run records (each with `workflow_run_id`, `head_sha`, `rc`, `terminal_state`) | **2,823 JSON** |
+| Frontier models actually invoked in CI | Claude Opus 5.5, GPT-5.6 Sol, Gemini 3.8 Flash, DeepSeek V4.1 Flash, plus local `brain-qwen3.5-9b`, SkillRouter-Reranker-0.6B, ettin-reranker-150m |
+
+The capsules are named after the project's whole history — `universal_learning_v5` through `v9`,
+`p1_v7_current_main`, `root2_v10`, `root3_minimum_action_cut_v1`, `tb_science_rank6…rank10`,
+`osworld_v21_official_projection`, `one_shot_reality_closure_v2`. This is the project's archaeology,
+and it is the reason the "answer against a frozen commit" is not a proposal: **403 frozen commits
+already exist**, each with the runtime that produced it.
+
+**Two corrections this forces:**
+
+1. **"$0, 0 model dependencies" is scoped to the `brain` solver, not the project.** The runner carries
+   `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `GOOGLE_API_KEY`, `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, `OPENROUTER_MANAGEMENT_API_KEY`, and
+   directories literally named `*_spent` (`agentdebugx_real_spent`, `cognitive_c3_skillrouter_spent`,
+   `atomic_root_cause_replay_spent`). Frontier models were run and paid for. What the records show is
+   that **capability credit** stayed zero, not that spend did.
+2. Every committed result carries `capability_credit_delta: 0` and
+   `status: MEASUREMENT_ONLY__…ZERO_CAPABILITY_CREDIT`. A run that succeeds — `terminal_state:
+   SUCCESS`, `rc: 0`, `root_step_accuracy: 1.0` — is still structurally forbidden from claiming
+   capability. **That is the strongest honesty invariant in the project, and it lives outside
+   `brain/`,** in a repo no report had read.
+
+## 2c. Two claims in §2b that this pass retracts
+
+**Retraction A — capsules are not "403 frozen snapshots of the whole runtime."**
+Measured: 403 capsules, **3,061 files total, median 7 files, max 33, min 1**. `universal_learning_v9`
+is 7 files / 33 KB. A capsule is an **overlay delta pinned by git blob SHA**, not a copy:
+
+```json
+"exact_brain_blobs": { "canonical/runtime/meta_learning_policy_v9.py": "0b65330f2b796e…" , … },
+"verified_v8_base": { "verifier_merge_commit": "c097af209497b00c…" }
+```
+
+That is *better* for audit than a zip (one file's content is verifiable by SHA-1 without the 214 MB
+tree) and *weaker* as a claim (it is not 403 runnable systems). Also worth noting: capsules were
+pinned against **feature branches** — `brain_ref: "feature/universal-learning-v9-meta-policy-20261004"`
+— not `main`.
+
+**Retraction B — "zero capability credit" is mostly a convention, not a check.**
+**799 Python files write `capability_credit_delta: 0`. Almost none verify it.** The genuine
+enforcement is thin and local:
+
+- `retrieval_live_instrumented_executor_v1.py:56` — a real guard:
+  `forbidden=("verified_sufficient","verified_witness","acceptance_credit","family_credit","capability_credit","ownership_credit","promotion_authority")`
+- `matched_scope_abductive_residual_execution_v1.py:42-43` — `assert out["capability_credit_delta"] == 0`
+- `saccr_credit_kernel.py:39,86` — `raise ValueError` on unsupported credit rating
+- one test asserting the receipt: `test_coding_tb4_frontier_consistency_v1.py:24`
+
+Roughly **one check per two hundred declarations**. My §2b statement that this is "enforced at the
+workflow layer, where it can't be edited away by a single patch" is **wrong** and is withdrawn.
+
+## 2d. The property that survives all nine passes
+
+The same defect appears at **every** layer, including this report:
+
+| layer | declarations | checks |
+|---|---|---|
+| `brain/` root docs claiming to be THE answer | **19** | 0 value indexes |
+| `CURRENT_TERMINAL_AUTHORITY_V1.json` acceptance numbers | **4 conflicting** | none reconciles them |
+| runner `capability_credit_delta: 0` | **799 files write it** | ~4 verify it |
+| my own reports | 8 passes of claims | **4 retractions so far** |
+
+The invariant this project is actually missing is not compression, not confinement, not the
+predicate at `meta_circular_organ_graph_v1.py:3953`. It is the **ratio of declarations to
+enforcements**. Every layer states its properties far more often than it tests them — and the
+analysis of the project reproduced the same ratio, which is why four of my eight conclusions had to
+be withdrawn.
+
+## 2e. The test asset — 16,976 tests, ~100 enforced, ~5% red
+
+Every earlier report ranked files by "test mass" and quoted test counts as evidence. None ran them.
+Measured on 2026-11-05:
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Test files in `canonical/tests` | **2,419** |
+| Tests **collected** | **16,976** |
+| Files that fail to collect (import errors) | **42** |
+| Workflows in `brain/.github/workflows` | **334** |
+| Workflows that invoke `pytest` | **53** |
+| Workflows that run `canonical/tests` **as a directory** | **0** |
+
+Every one of the 53 pytest workflows names 1–3 specific files. **No job anywhere runs the suite.**
+The figure "2,365 test subjects" used in earlier reports was distinct test-*name* stems; the real
+count is 7× larger and 84% of it is never executed by CI.
+
+A full-suite run (`-n 2`, `--timeout=180`, `--continue-on-collection-errors`) reached **99% in
+25 minutes and then never terminated** — a handful of tests hang past their timeout, and xdist
+restarts workers, duplicating outcomes. Among ~15,900 reported outcomes: **~990 failures ≈ 5.3%**,
+~85% pass, 77 skipped, 1 xfail. The exact total is not cleanly attributable because of the worker
+restarts, and that is itself the finding: **this suite cannot be run to completion on a 2-core
+machine**, which is presumably why nobody does.
+
+## 3. What this answers
+
+**"Is this all the valuable things?"** No — and further sweeps will keep finding machinery without
+changing the finding. The answer is a **state census**, not an inventory:
+
+- **Machinery**: abundant, mapped (3,088 committed paths; ~19 irreducible for a published number).
+- **Evidence**: strong (578 external runs, 1,104 mission receipts, 780 intents).
+- **Measured capability**: 47.22% in-scope, 14/37 families, 490 addressable.
+- **Accumulated learning**: ~50 records, 9 of 12 memory entries dead.
+- **Off-repo assets**: two public repositories — `brain` (214 MB) and
+  **`verification-capsule-runner` (403 frozen capsules, 1,089 workflows, 480k LOC, 2,823 run records)**
+  — plus a Google Drive mirror whose address and hash are pinned in
+  `canonical/astra_runtime/artifacts/CANONICAL_POINTER_20260927.ubj`
+  (folder `1kdecUMm_qDEcAT95a_MF7EVsF08GQ0kwi`, snapshot `PROJECT_BRAIN_CANONICAL_SNAPSHOT_2026-09-21.zip`,
+  sha256 `000606bc93206eea…c01b0162`). Addressable and hash-verifiable; not retrievable from here.
+
+## 4. The boundary of this answer, stated so it can be checked
+
+Knowable from here: every file, every receipt, every intent, every test, the merge history, the
+persistent state. **Not** knowable from here: the Drive mirror; 6,252 earlier merges (readable, but
+they cannot restore a memory entry); 887 open issues (dominant class is auto-filed LiveBench
+diagnostics); anything held privately outside these two repositories.
+
+## 5. What is actually worth doing next
+
+Not a seventh inventory. The memory layer is small, 75% dead, and credits dead referents:
+
+1. **Prune or resolve the 9 dead associative entries** and refuse credit to any entry whose referent
+   does not resolve. That is a resolution check in one place, and it is the same discipline
+   `verifier_falsification_v1` already applies to verifiers.
+2. **Re-run the 11-04 concept-growth measurement** against the current tree — `G_t` admission is
+   UNKNOWN, not open (corrected in `VALUE_INDEX_20261105_V2.md` §1).
+3. **Populate `compiled_workflows_v1` from real solves.** It has a schema, eight columns, and zero
+   rows. The learning loop is built and empty.
+
+The machine's most valuable missing asset is not a document. It is three tables with rows in them.
