+# The heartbeat cancels itself
+
+**2026-11-05.** Thirty-first pass. Every number I have quoted for thirty passes — including the one I
+called decisive — comes from one workflow. That workflow has **583 runs: 106 success, 95 failure, 382
+cancelled.** Its last success was **2026-10-19T19:31:41Z**, 17 days ago. Its last twenty runs are
+**20/20 cancelled**, including today's scheduled run at 10:50Z. I tried to reproduce the number locally
+and the instrument failed in 32 seconds.
+**Authority: NONE. Credit: 0.**
+
+---
+
+## 1. The number I have been quoting
+
+```
+live_solver_end_to_end_measurement_v1.py · seed 435920808002669906 · 37 families x 5
+OLD 36.67 %  →  NEW 47.22 %  ·  14/37  ·  model_dependency_count 0  ·  spend $0
+```
+
+This is the project's headline capability result. It is the "measured" side of the ledger every plan and
+audit in this project rests on: *27 of 141 bound capabilities measured working end to end.*
+
+## 2. Its only producer, measured
+
+`.github/workflows/live-brain-heartbeat.yml` is the sole workflow that invokes the instrument
+(1 of 712 workflows). GitHub API, whole history:
+
+| conclusion | runs |
+|---|---:|
+| success | **106** |
+| failure | 95 |
+| cancelled | **382** |
+| timed out | 0 |
+| **total** | **583** |
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| last success | run **#295**, `2026-10-19T19:31:41Z` |
+| days since | **17** |
+| last 20 runs | **cancelled: 20** |
+| today's scheduled run | #583, `2026-11-05T10:50:49Z`, **cancelled** |
+
+## 3. The cause is in the configuration
+
+```yaml
+concurrency:
+  group: live-brain-heartbeat-${{ github.ref }}
+  cancel-in-progress: true
+...
+    timeout-minutes: 40
+```
+
+The workflow's own comment states the measurement cost:
+
+> *37 families × 50 = 1,850 in-scope + 100 out-of-scope … ~49 minutes of work for ~2 minutes of census …
+> The job was therefore cancelled on 17 of the last 20 runs — five daily schedule runs in a row — and
+> because the step never finished, the artifact upload then failed too, **so no receipt and no summary
+> survived.***
+
+So: a long measurement, `cancel-in-progress: true`, one concurrency group **per ref**, in a repository
+taking ~36 merges/day. Every PR-triggered run of the same ref kills the in-flight scheduled run before it
+can upload. The workflow was revised to halve its work (`--entries new`, `--jobs 4`) with the note
+*"Speed by removing duplicated work, not by verifying less"* — and **the revised version has never once
+completed**: the last success precedes the fix's own recorded measurement date of 2026-10-27.
+
+## 4. What I did about it
+
+I ran the instrument on today's tree, same seed, same family budget:
+
+```
+$ python3 execution_guard/live_solver_end_to_end_measurement_v1.py \
+    --seed 435920808002669906 --per-family 5 --jobs 4
+{"error": "EDIT_PLAN_INPUT_INVALID", "error_kind": "systemic",
+ "message": "source_root is not a directory: ab_optional_inputs_20261030.py"}
+```
+
+32 seconds, no measurements, systemic. The fixture builder maps `source_root` to a directory
+(`work/"src"`), yet the plan compiler receives a *filename*. So the headline number is, on today's `main`:
+
+- **not produced** (17 days, 20/20 recent runs cancelled),
+- **not persisted** — no receipt on `main` contains `run_complete`; no file in the tree contains the seed,
+- **not reproducible locally** — systemic input-typing failure at the first affected capability.
+
+It also **mutates tracked state**: the attempt left `canonical/runtime/state/experience_v1.json` modified
+in the working tree (restored with `git checkout`). The measurement is therefore not read-only — each
+attempt dirties the repository, which is itself incompatible with reproducible re-measurement.
+
+I state the honest caveat: the local failure could be an environment requirement I did not satisfy, and
+106 historical successes exist. But all three facts above are measured, and any one of them alone is
+enough to mean the number cannot be re-derived by a fresh clone today.
+
+## 5. Correction of my own reporting
+
+I have cited this number as decisive for twenty-plus passes. It is **17 days old, unpersisted, and
+unreproducible**, and I never tested it once. Meanwhile I spent thirty passes measuring the project's
+*governance* for staleness — 305 blob pins going stale at 36 merges/day — while the one number everything
+was built on went stale in the same way and I quoted it as current every time.
+
+That is the third self-correction of this session (after the interlock and the unclicked button), and the
+most consequential: **the thing I treated as my anchor was the least verified fact I had.**
+
+## 6. What it costs to fix
+
+Two defects, both small and both named:
+
+1. **One line of concurrency config.** Schedule runs must not share a cancellation group with
+   PR-triggered runs (`cancel-in-progress: false` for `schedule`, or a group keyed on
+   `github.event_name`). A daily measurement that is killed by every push in a repo with 36 merges/day
+   can never complete by construction.
+2. **One input-typing bug.** `source_root` must be materialised as a directory before it reaches the
+   edit-plan compiler; `ab_optional_inputs_20261030.py` is a file being passed where a directory is
+   required.
+
+## 7. The answer
+
+**No — this is not all of them, and the most important thing is that the project's headline result
+cannot currently be produced.**
+
+Not missing, not unmerged, not uncredited — **unreproduced**. Thirty-one passes have charted a project
+whose central measurement is 17 days stale, whose receipt book is empty, whose only producer is
+configured to cancel itself, and whose instrument no longer runs on its own tree. Everything downstream —
+141 bound capabilities, 27 measured, 348 unmerged pairs passing, 300/300 contract cases, 4,144 merged PRs
+— inherits that number's uncertainty.
+
+The valuable things are real: the substrate installs, the contracts score, the reducer authorises, the
+unmerged code runs. But the *rate* that makes any of it a claim about capability is 17 days old and
+recorded nowhere. Fixing that is one concurrency key and one path type — and unlike everything else this
+session has found, it is a change that would make the project's own numbers true again rather than
+better described.
