+# Fourteen sessions have already answered this question
+
+**2026-11-05.** Twenty-seventh pass. Previous passes counted files, refs, capabilities, tests and
+branches. This one reads what the other concurrent sessions concluded — and finds that the question I
+have been answering for twenty-six passes has been answered independently, many times, with the same
+conclusion, and none of it is on `main`.
+**Authority: NONE. Credit: 0.**
+
+---
+
+## 1. What the concurrent sessions produced
+
+Of the 52 `arena/*` branches, **14 sessions wrote reports** — 72 documents that exist nowhere on `main`:
+
+| theme | count |
+|---|---:|
+| first-principles pass (one session's 30-pass series) | 30 |
+| plans ("the optimal plan" V1→V9, one-shot plans, real-now plans) | 10 |
+| **censuses of limiting factors / first-principles audits** | **5** |
+| handoffs | 2 |
+| other measured reports | 25 |
+
+Sessions by output: `3c70152b` 36 · `b0d725c0` 10 · `b266b92a` 5 · `01a0f44a` 4 · `086851e2` 4 ·
+`9672736d` 3 · `0e27dc1b` 2 · `e3edbfbb` 2 · and five more with one each.
+
+Five of these are explicitly what I have been producing for twenty-six passes:
+
+```
+Complete enumeration of limiting factors between the current state and the terminal goal — V2
+Complete ledger of limiting factors — terminal checkpoint OPUS_5_5_USEFUL_CAPABILITY_OWNERSHIP
+FIRST-PRINCIPLES AUDIT — the whole Brain, deepest layer first (2026-10-16)
+First-principles audit — 2026-10-16 (measurements, not opinions)
+The repair organ's real ceiling, and what the honesty gate can actually see
+```
+
+## 2. They converge — on the operator, not the machine
+
+Independent sessions, different methods, different dates, same conclusion:
+
+| session | its conclusion |
+|---|---|
+| `3c70152b` pass 4 | *"the learner is me, and the creature was starved"* |
+| `3c70152b` pass 8 | *"the ceiling was a constant I chose"* |
+| `3c70152b` pass 16 | *"the deepest layer was that I was the only thing learning"* |
+| `3c70152b` pass 22 | *"the creature was carrying a false belief about itself"* |
+| `b0d725c0` round 28 | *"the instrument was lying, and the abstraction was a bin"* |
+| `b0d725c0` round 29 | *"the language was a list I typed"* |
+| `b0d725c0` round 30 | *"the degree was also mine"* |
+| `b0d725c0` round 27 | *"a self-model that never observed itself"* |
+| `b266b92a` | *"the creature is built, tested, and never started"* |
+
+Nine statements, six sessions, one finding: **every ceiling measured is authored by the operator.**
+That is the same conclusion my own enumeration reached by a different route — pass 9's
+"declarations outnumber enforcements ~200:1", pass 7's "~50 records of learning, 9 of 12 memory
+entries dead", pass 24's "the project does not lack the checks, it lacks the merge".
+
+## 3. The actual limiting factor
+
+`main` holds:
+
+- **19** root documents claiming to be THE answer
+- **0** value indexes
+- **4** conflicting acceptance counts inside a single authority file
+- **305** pinned blob SHAs that go stale at 36 merges/day
+- and, now measured, **five independent censuses of its own limiting factors and ten plans** — none
+  merged.
+
+The project does not suffer from a shortage of analysis. It generates analysis faster than it
+consolidates it: fourteen sessions, seventy-two reports, a thousand-odd tested modules, and 43% of the
+files off `main`. My twenty-six passes are simply the most recent instance of the pattern, not an
+exception to it.
+
+## 4. The answer to the question as asked
+
+**No — it is not all of them, and the inventory is not what is missing.**
+
+The honest content of "everything valuable and important in the whole project", measured:
+
+| layer | figure |
+|---|---|
+| `main`, both repos | 22,916 files, partitioned, 0 unclassified |
+| all refs | 21,332 refs · 73,761 commits · 43% of files branch-only |
+| unmerged work, executed | 348 / 1,188 module+test pairs pass in isolation |
+| capabilities | 141 bound · 27 measured · 118 never exercised |
+| accumulated learning | ~50 records · 9 of 12 memory entries dead |
+| independent verification | 18 / 18 external runs real · idle since 2026-10-12 |
+| concurrent analysis | 14 sessions · 72 reports · 5 censuses · 0 merged |
+| reproducibility | hash-pinned substrate installs from a clean clone · undocumented |
+
+The set can always be extended by one more file, ref, or report — which is why twenty-seven passes of
+"is this all" have each produced a true *no*. But the load-bearing fact is not that the list is
+incomplete. It is that **fourteen independent agents have measured this system and reached the same
+finding, and the finding has never been acted on.**
+
+The next question worth asking is not "is this everything". It is "which single merge would change the
+answer" — and by the measurements in this file there are two candidates: the anti-drift interlock that
+refuses stale authority, and the creature-learning work in `3c70152b` that took thirty passes to make
+experience transfer.
