+## 7. One paragraph for the owner
+
+What you have that is real: a working, honest, model-free execution core — a 443-capability
+registry behind one byte-deterministic front door, a plain-English compiler that really does land
+on verified execution, nine kernels that reproduce PASS on instances nobody chose, and a process
+that survives being killed. All of it measured, all of it $0, none of it independent yet. What you
+do **not** have, measured by your own instruments: compounding learning (0/10 across kinds), model
+independence in 15 of 19 capability families, a green suite (789 real failures), or any terminal
+credit. The gap between those two paragraphs is not dishonesty — it is the backlog, and it is
+written down in more detail than any project I have seen. The most valuable thing in the repository
+is the part that refuses to let the first paragraph be confused with the second. Protect it.
