+### 2.3 The deepest open defect — **still open in live code; I verified it**
+
+`THE_DEEPEST_STILL_OPEN_DEFECT_NOTHING_IS_EVER_COMPRESSED` says the concept library `G_t` never
+grows because `_skill_organ_to_concept_entry` admits only an organ whose body is a single `return`
+expression. **That predicate is still there today**, at
+`canonical/swe_kernel/meta_circular_organ_graph_v1.py:3953`:
+
+```python
+if not (len(fn.body) == 1 and isinstance(fn.body[0], ast.Return) and fn.body[0].value is not None):
+    return None
+```
+
+The synthesizer emits `Assign, Assign, Return` — three statements — so the bridge rejects every organ
+it produces, silently. **The library is empty, `G_t` never grows, and no experience can compound.**
+Everything the project is *for* — "gets better at new problems because it has met old ones" — is
+blocked on one formatting assumption masquerading as a safety check. This is the single highest-value
+defect in the repository and it is one function away from being fixable. See §6.1.
+
+### 2.4 The bound capability surface + one front door — 443 executable identities, 490 addressable
